<script nonce="4IR0yGWICShHhZzLY48rnw==">
// Statement overlay — opens from the right on .statement-link click
(function () {
  var overlay   = document.getElementById('stmtOverlay');
  var titleEl   = document.getElementById('stmtOverlayTitle');
  var contentEl = document.getElementById('stmtOverlayContent');
  if (!overlay) return;

  var statements = {
    uoss: {
      title: 'CGS License for End User Customers',
      body: [
        'An end user customer generally refers to a recipient of data originating from CUSIP Global Services&rsquo; ("CGS") databases, products or services ("CGS Data") who receives the benefit of CGS Data for usage within its internal operations or to support its internal business processes. Internal operations and internal business processes do not include further onward distribution of CGS Data to third parties or commercialization of CGS Data. CGS Data includes CUSIP, CINS, CGS ISIN identifiers, and any other identifiers issued by CGS (collectively referred to as "CGS Identifiers"), plus <span class="stmt-tip">additional information about financial instruments originating from CGS&rsquo;s databases<span class="stmt-tip-box">Up to 60+ additional data attributes including standardized issuer / issue descriptions, maturity date(s), rates, issue dates, payment frequency, tickers, currency and related industry standards such as the Financial Instrument Short Name (FISN) description and the Classification of Financial Instruments (CFI) code.</span></span>.',
        'Authorized Data Vendors supply services to indirect end user customers and typically fall within the following two categories: (i) information vendors, data vendors or information service providers who furnish the benefit of CGS Data to indirect end user customers through the usage and incorporation of CGS Data as part of their own products or services, and (ii) outsourcing providers who furnish the benefit of CGS Data to indirect end user customers through some type of outsourced or managed solution (e.g., business process outsourcing; back-office outsourcing; trade processing; portfolio accounting; trust and fund accounting, or fund administration, as well as various other hosted, outsourced or managed solutions that offer middle-to-back-office "software as a service" solutions).',
        '<h4 class="stmt-overlay-subhead">CUSIP Use of Service Statement for End User Customers</h4>',
        'The first step in the CGS licensing process for end user customers is to complete and return a <a href="https://www.cusip.com/pdf/CUSIP_Global_Services-Useof_Service_Statement.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CUSIP Use of Service Statement ("UOSS")</a>. The UOSS allows CGS to understand how a potential end user customer plans on accessing, using, storing, processing or otherwise benefitting from the CGS Data. The UOSS enables CGS to continue its longstanding practice of treating beneficiaries of CGS Data fairly and on a level playing field to maintain parity. By fully and accurately completing the UOSS, the end user customer ensures that its license fees are calculated based on the benefit it receives from the CGS Data and that such fees are fair, reasonable and non-discriminatory.',
        '<h4 class="stmt-overlay-subhead">CGS Identifiers</h4>',
        'CGS Identifiers include CUSIPs, CGS ISINs, CGS CINS and any other identifier issued by CGS. All CGS ISINs are embedded with either a CUSIP Identifier or a CINS Identifier. When a database contains both a CGS ISIN, and its embedded CUSIP or CINS separately, they shall be collectively counted as one unique CGS Identifier.',
        'Below are definitions for each CGS Identifier. When it comes to identifying CGS ISINs, please use the International Organization for Standardization (ISO) Prefixes provided below to properly identify CGS ISINs.',
        '(i) CUSIP (Committee on Uniform Security Identification Procedures) Identifier: a 9-character alphanumeric identifier assigned for issuers and their financial instruments offered in the U.S. and Canada.',
        '(ii) CINS (CUSIP International Number System) Identifier: a 9-character alphanumeric identifier that uses the same 9-character format as CUSIP identifiers and is the local identifier of more than 30 non-North American markets.',
        '(iii) CGS ISIN (International Securities Identification Number) Identifier: a 12-character global identifier assigned by CGS in its role as National Numbering Agency for the United States and substitute National Numbering Agency for selected countries.',
        'The ISO Prefixes for CGS ISINs are as follows:',
        'US, CA, KY, BM, VI, VG, UM, TT, SR, GS, SX, VC, MF, LC, KN, BL, PR, PH, PW, MP, FM, YT, MH, HT, GY, GU, GD, DM, CW, BQ, BZ, BS, AW, AG, AI, AS, AN',
        'For more information on the global standard, please visit <a href="https://www.anna-web.org/standards/isin-iso-6166/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://www.anna-web.org/standards/isin-iso-6166/</a>'
      ]
    },
    eul: {
      title: 'CGS License Structure for End User Customers',
      body: [
        '<h4 class="stmt-overlay-subhead">End User</h4>',
        'The CGS License Fees applicable to end user customers who receive the benefits of CGS Data are based primarily on three (3) criteria: 1) the number of unique CGS Identifiers accessed, stored, maintained, processed or otherwise used by or for the benefit of an end user customer (all such types of usage, whether individually or in any combination thereof, shall be collectively referred to as "Used", "Used by" or "Usage of", or a similar variation thereof); 2) the number of Business Lines with Usage of CGS Data; and 3) the number of Regions with Usage of CGS Data. CGS Data includes CUSIP, CINS, CGS ISIN Identifiers, and any other identifiers issued by CGS (collectively referred to as "CGS Identifiers"), plus <span class="stmt-tip">additional information about financial instruments originating from CGS&rsquo;s databases<span class="stmt-tip-box">Up to 60+ additional data attributes including standardized issuer / issue descriptions, maturity date(s), rates, issue dates, payment frequency, tickers, currency and related industry standards such as the Financial Instrument Short Name (FISN) description and the Classification of Financial Instruments (CFI) code.</span></span>.',
        '<h4 class="stmt-overlay-subhead">Determining the Count of Unique CGS Identifiers</h4>',
        'The count of CGS Identifiers should include all unique CGS Identifiers that an end user customer ultimately receives the benefit of in order to support or operate any part of its internal business processes or operations, regardless of where such CGS Identifiers are Used. This count applies whether: (i) the CGS Data received by an end user customer is Used directly by the end user customer, or (ii) the end user customer receives the benefit of CGS Data being Used as part of some type of outsourced or managed solution.',
        '<h4 class="stmt-overlay-subhead">Examples</h4>',
        '<p class="stmt-example"><span class="stmt-num">1.</span><strong>Use of CGS Data in selecting securities of interest.</strong> An end user customer may Use 5,000 CGS Identifiers, which reflects only those securities in which it <span class="stmt-tip">holds, or at one time held<span class="stmt-tip-box">This applies to accounting only use cases</span></span> a position. However, if an end user customer&rsquo;s own internal business processes entails Usage of 30,000 CGS Identifiers to perform its business processes (e.g. quantitative/qualitative/systematic research, trade processing, programmatic trading, performance measurement, attribution analysis, benchmarking, risk analysis, portfolio analytics, reconciliation, quantitative analysis, etc.), to select those 5,000 CGS Identifiers, it is the universe of 30,000 CGS Identifiers that should be counted. Conversely, if an end user customer receives a data feed or similar bulk distribution that includes 30,000 CGS Identifiers, but the Use is limited to only 5,000 CGS Identifiers in which it <span class="stmt-tip">holds, or at one time held<span class="stmt-tip-box">This applies to accounting only use cases</span></span> a position, then it&rsquo;s the 5,000 CGS Identifiers that should be counted.</p>',
        '<p class="stmt-example"><span class="stmt-num">2.</span><strong>Use of CGS Data in <span class="stmt-tip">accounting systems<span class="stmt-tip-box"><strong>Please note:</strong> This example specifically applies to accounting-only use-cases.</span></span>.</strong> An end user customer may Use 10,000 CGS Identifiers in its accounting system, which reflects those securities in which it <span class="stmt-tip">holds, or at one time held<span class="stmt-tip-box">This applies to accounting only use cases</span></span> a position. However, if an end user customer needs access to the accounting system for securities transactions greater than 12 months old in order to fulfil statutory audit requirements, regulatory compliance purposes, or is required by law, then the count may be limited to 12 months of securities transaction history (including any long-term holdings). Conversely, if an end user customer needs to Use 20,000 CGS Identifiers in order to perform its own internal business processes, in order to select 10,000 securities in which it holds, or has held a position; it is the universe of 20,000 CGS Identifiers that should be counted.</p>',
        '<p class="stmt-example"><span class="stmt-num">3.</span><strong>Use of CGS Data in an outsourced or managed solution.</strong> An end user customer may receive the benefit of CGS Data through the outsourcing of its internal business operations or processes to an Authorized Data Vendor (e.g., trade processing, portfolio accounting, portfolio analytics, trust and fund accounting, fund administration, reconciliation, performance measurement, risk analytics, regulatory reporting, etc.). The internal business processes of the end user customer are effectively being performed by the Authorized Data Vendor, who as part of its service, is otherwise performing and/or supporting the internal business operations or processes on behalf of and for the benefit of the end user customer. In these circumstances, the end user customer is a beneficiary of the CGS Data and therefore, Usage of CGS Data is attributed to that end user customer and, separately, there may be instances where an Authorized Data Vendor has an independent and distinct use of CGS Data depending on their level of service. Please refer to Examples 1 and 2 for guidance as to how to count the number of CGS Identifiers.</p>'
      ]
    },
    adv: {
      title: 'Authorized Data Vendors',
      body: [
        'Authorized Data Vendors supply services to indirect end user customers and typically fall within the following two categories: (i) information vendors, data vendors or information service providers who furnish the benefit of CGS Data to indirect end user customers through the usage and incorporation of CGS Data as part of their own products or services, and (ii) outsourcing providers who furnish the benefit of CGS Data to indirect end user customers through some type of outsourced or managed solution (e.g., business process outsourcing; back-office outsourcing; trade processing; portfolio accounting; trust and fund accounting, or fund administration, as well as various other hosted, outsourced or managed solutions that offer middle-to-back-office "software as a service" solutions).',
        '<a href="/contact.html">Please contact a CGS Representative for information regarding the fees and terms applicable to Authorized Data Vendors.</a>'
      ]
    }
  };

  function open(key) {
    var st = statements[key];
    if (!st) return;
    titleEl.innerHTML = st.title;
    var html = st.body.map(function (p) {
      return /^\s*<(h4|ul|ol|p)\b/.test(p) ? p : '<p>' + p + '</p>';
    }).join('');
    if (st.doc) {
      html += '<a class="stmt-overlay-doc" href="' + st.doc[1] + '" target="_blank" rel="noopener">' + st.doc[0] +
              '</a>';
    }
    contentEl.innerHTML = html;
    overlay.classList.add('open');
    overlay.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'false');
    document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
  }
  function close() {
    overlay.classList.remove('open');
    overlay.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
    document.body.style.overflow = '';
  }

  document.querySelectorAll('.statement-link').forEach(function (link) {
    link.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
      e.preventDefault();
      open(link.dataset.statement);
    });
  });
  overlay.querySelectorAll('[data-close]').forEach(function (el) { el.addEventListener('click', close); });
  document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
    if (e.key === 'Escape' && overlay.classList.contains('open')) close();
  });
})();

// ── End User Fee Estimator ──
(function () {
  var modal = document.getElementById('feeModal');
  if (!modal) return;
  var openBtn = document.getElementById('feeEstimatorBtn');
  var closeBtn = document.getElementById('feeModalClose');
  var resetBtn = document.getElementById('feeReset');
  var totalEl = document.getElementById('feeTotal');
  var fIdent = document.getElementById('feeIdentifiers');
  var fLines = document.getElementById('feeLines');
  var fRegions = document.getElementById('feeRegions');
  var fDiscount = document.getElementById('feeDiscount');

  // Mirrors the authoritative FeeCalculator formula in /js/app.js (data-fee-calculator),
  // truncating to a whole number after each percentage increase.
  function fmt(n) {
    return '$' + Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US');
  }

  var descEl = document.getElementById('feeDiscountDesc');

  // Mirrors the discount descriptions in getDiscountDesc() in /js/app.js, keyed by
  // the tier number in each <option value="rate_tier"> (e.g. "50_9" -> "9").
  var discountDescriptions = {
    '0': 'Institutions that obtain data originating from a CGS Database via an electronic data feed or bulk download, solely to fulfill governmental regulatory reporting requirements, are eligible for a no-fee license.',
    '1': 'Non-Financial Research, including publishing, consulting, or not-for-profit, are eligible for a 75% discount on fees.',
    '2': 'U.S. Only Small Banks with total bank assets less than $1B are eligible for a 90% discount on fees.',
    '3': 'U.S. Only Mid-sized Banks with total bank assets between $1B-$10B are eligible for a 50% discount on fees.',
    '4': 'Small Asset Managers with assets under management less than $5B are eligible for a 50% discount on fees.',
    '5': 'U.S. Only Regional Broker-Dealers, whose main operations, and the majority of its customers, are located in a single state or sub-region are eligible for a 30% discount on fees.',
    '6': 'Government entities and Regulators, including central banks, state owned pension funds, state or federal agency (excludes sovereign wealth funds) are eligible for a 50% discount on fees.',
    '7': 'Academic institutions with non-commercial academic research and teaching objectives are eligible for a 100% discount on fees.',
    '8': 'University Endowments with assets under management less than $5B are eligible for a 50% discount on fees.',
    '9': 'Limited Asset Class, including municipal bonds only, corporate bonds only, structured finance only are eligible for a 50% discount on fees.',
    '10': 'U.S. Only Wealth Managers with assets under management less than $5B are eligible for a 100% discount on fees. CGS defines wealth management as firms that provide financial planning, comprehensive wealth services, manager due diligence, asset allocation and investment selection advice to clients. Wealth managers may offer holistic planning including accounting services, tax and estate planning and family office services. This definition does not include other segments within the RIA market such as banks, broker/dealers, hedge funds or asset managers.',
    '11': 'Asset Managers with micro assets under management less than $500M are eligible for a 90% discount on fees.',
    '12': 'Equity Only firms are eligible for special flat pricing for securities counts over 20,000. Standard list price applies for up to 20,000 securities.'
  };

  function updateDiscountDesc() {
    if (!descEl) return;
    var discountCode = fDiscount.value || 'none';
    var descKey = discountCode === 'none' ? null : discountCode.split('_')[1];
    var desc = descKey !== null ? discountDescriptions[descKey] : null;
    if (desc) {
      descEl.textContent = desc;
      descEl.classList.add('visible');
    } else {
      descEl.textContent = '';
      descEl.classList.remove('visible');
    }
  }

  // Only Micro AUM / U.S. Only Small Bank discounts apply to the "Under 2,500" tier.
  function syncDiscountOptions() {
    var isSmallTier = +fIdent.value === 10500;
    var options = fDiscount.querySelectorAll('option[data-tiers]');
    var needsReset = false;
    options.forEach(function (opt) {
      var allowed = !isSmallTier || opt.getAttribute('data-tiers') === 'all';
      opt.disabled = !allowed;
      if (!allowed && opt.selected) needsReset = true;
    });
    if (needsReset) fDiscount.value = 'none';
  }

  function calc() {
    syncDiscountOptions();
    updateDiscountDesc();

    if (fIdent.value === '' || fLines.value === '' || fRegions.value === '') {
      totalEl.innerHTML = '&mdash;';
      return;
    }

    var securitiesValue = +fIdent.value;
    var businessLinesValue = +fLines.value;
    var regionsValue = +fRegions.value;
    var discountCode = fDiscount.value || 'none';

    if (securitiesValue === 1) {
      totalEl.textContent = 'Fee Waived';
      return;
    }

    if (securitiesValue >= 21000 && discountCode === '00_0') {
      totalEl.textContent = 'Fee Waived';
      return;
    }

    var discountParts = discountCode.split('_');

    var total = 0;
    for (var i = 1; i <= regionsValue; i++) {
      for (var j = 1; j <= businessLinesValue; j++) {
        total += securitiesValue / (i === 3 ? 4 : i) / (j === 3 ? 4 : j);
      }
    }

    var total1 = Math.floor(Math.floor(total) * 1.055);   // 5.5% increase
    var total2 = Math.floor(total1 * 1.028);              // 2.8% increase
    var total3 = Math.floor(total2 * 1.028);              // 2.8% increase on 2/2/2026

    // Equity Only: flat pricing (base 76092) for tiers over 20,000; standard list price otherwise.
    if (discountParts[1] === '12') {
      if (securitiesValue === 94500 || securitiesValue === 126000 || securitiesValue === 136500) {
        var equityBase = 76092;
        var equityTotal = 0;
        for (var ei = 1; ei <= regionsValue; ei++) {
          for (var ej = 1; ej <= businessLinesValue; ej++) {
            equityTotal += equityBase / (ei === 3 ? 4 : ei) / (ej === 3 ? 4 : ej);
          }
        }
        totalEl.textContent = fmt(Math.floor(equityTotal));
        return;
      }
      totalEl.textContent = fmt(total3);
      return;
    }

    var discountsValue = discountCode === 'none' ? 0 : +discountParts[0];

    var result = discountsValue !== 0
      ? Math.floor(total3 - (total3 * discountsValue / 100))
      : total3;

    totalEl.textContent = result < 1 ? 'Fee Waived' : fmt(result);
  }

  function openModal(e) {
    if (e) e.preventDefault();
    modal.classList.add('active');
    document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
  }
  function closeModal() {
    modal.classList.remove('active');
    document.body.style.overflow = '';
  }
  function reset() {
    fIdent.value = ''; fLines.value = ''; fRegions.value = ''; fDiscount.value = 'none';
    fDiscount.querySelectorAll('option[data-tiers]').forEach(function (opt) { opt.disabled = false; });
    totalEl.innerHTML = '&mdash;';
    updateDiscountDesc();
  }

  document.querySelectorAll('.feeEstimatorOpen').forEach(function (b) { b.addEventListener('click', openModal); });
  closeBtn.addEventListener('click', closeModal);
  resetBtn.addEventListener('click', reset);
  modal.addEventListener('click', function (e) { if (e.target === modal) closeModal(); });
  document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
    if (e.key === 'Escape' && modal.classList.contains('active')) closeModal();
  });
  [fIdent, fLines, fRegions, fDiscount].forEach(function (el) {
    el.addEventListener('change', calc);
  });
})();
</script>
<script type="text/javascript" nonce="4IR0yGWICShHhZzLY48rnw==">
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
     document.addEventListener('click', function(e) {
        var link = e.target.closest('[data-redirect]');
        if (link) {
           e.preventDefault();
           var redirectType = link.getAttribute('data-redirect');
           if (typeof redirectUrl === 'function') {
              redirectUrl(redirectType);
           }
        }

        var closeBtn = e.target.closest('[data-close-calculator]');
        if (closeBtn) {
           var calcId = closeBtn.getAttribute('data-close-calculator');
           var calc = document.getElementById(calcId);
           if (calc) {
              calc.classList.remove('is-open');
           }
        }
     });

     var searchInput = document.getElementById('searchByKeyword');
     if (searchInput) {
        searchInput.addEventListener('keypress', function(event) {
           if (typeof searchTextFn === 'function') {
              searchTextFn(event);
           }
        });
     }
  });
</script>



<script nonce="4IR0yGWICShHhZzLY48rnw==">
// ── FAQ Accordion ──
document.querySelectorAll('.faq-accordion .faq-q').forEach(function(btn) {
  btn.addEventListener('click', function() {
    var accordion = btn.closest('.faq-accordion');
    var item = btn.closest('.faq-item');
    if (!accordion || !item) return;
    var isOpen = item.classList.contains('open');

    accordion.querySelectorAll('.faq-item').forEach(function(el) {
      el.classList.remove('open');
      var q = el.querySelector('.faq-q');
      var body = el.querySelector('.faq-body');
      if (q) q.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
      if (body) body.hidden = true;
    });

    if (!isOpen) {
      item.classList.add('open');
      btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
      var panel = item.querySelector('.faq-body');
      if (panel) panel.hidden = false;
    }
  });
});

(function () {
  const modal = document.getElementById('disclaimerModal');
  const closeBtn = document.getElementById('modalClose');
  const continueBtn = document.getElementById('modalContinue');
  if (!modal || !closeBtn || !continueBtn) return;
  let pendingHref = null;

  function openModal(href) {
    pendingHref = href;
    modal.classList.add('active');
    document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
  }

  function closeModal() {
    modal.classList.remove('active');
    document.body.style.overflow = '';
    pendingHref = null;
  }

  // Intercept all card links
  document.querySelectorAll('.apply-card-links a').forEach(function (link) {
    link.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
      e.preventDefault();
      openModal(link.getAttribute('href'));
    });
  });

  closeBtn.addEventListener('click', closeModal);

  continueBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
    closeModal();
    if (pendingHref && pendingHref !== '#') {
      window.location.href = pendingHref;
    }
  });

  // Close on overlay click
  modal.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
    if (e.target === modal) closeModal();
  });

  // Close on Escape
  document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
    if (e.key === 'Escape') closeModal();
  });
}());
</script>
</body>
</html>
